Luc Besson rejects the idea that he reinvented action cinema. He simply used to have the freedom to experiment.

&#x201C;When you don&#x2019;t have a lot of experience, you have all this freedom. You aren&#x2019;t controlled by big studios and 50 people telling you why you can&#x2019;t do something because it costs too much. For about 20 years now, people with money have taken control of cinema. They say: &#x2018;I pay, so I decide.&#x2019; No. The one who decides is the creator.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories 'Wanted' Broadway Review: Dazzling Cast Can't Elevate the Musical’s Muted Narrative Geese’s Soaring Live Show Lives Up to the Hype, With Fearless Improvisations and Boundless Energy: Concert Review

&#x201C;When Modigliani wanted to paint women with long necks and black eyes, that&#x2019;s what he did. We need to take this freedom back because we are simply killing art. We&#x2019;re turning it into something that can be sold, like yogurt or socks. There are four crucial things in the lives of men and women: Water, air, love and art. Without them, we&#x2019;re dead.&#x201D;

He added, &#x201C;Now, we have replaced everything with money. And it&#x2019;s going to kill us all.&#x201D;

Besson was speaking at Torino Film Festival , where he received the Stella delle Mole award for lifetime achievement. Earlier that day, he deadpanned, &#x201C;I saw the list of all the people who have received it, and I didn&#x2019;t understand why I hadn&#x2019;t received it too. I&#x2019;m not used to receiving awards in my own country, so I&#x2019;m happy to receive one abroad.&#x201D;

Celebrated for &#x201C;The Big Blue,&#x201D; &#x201C;L&#xE9;on: The Professional,&#x201D; &#x201C; The Fifth Element &#x201D; and &#x201C;Lucy,&#x201D; Besson was honest about his preferences.

&#x201C;Some directors are very good at making films about their neighbors &#x2013; I don&#x2019;t know how to do that. I like extraordinary stories. I make films to wander, to disappear and explore other worlds. I don&#x2019;t want to tell the story of my neighbor. I want to tell the story of a guy who drives a taxi in the 23rd century,&#x201D; he said, referencing Bruce Willis&#x2019; role in &#x201C;The Fifth Element.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;These characters are always a little bit broken by society, always on the margins. Also, I like to explore the strength of women and the weakness of men. If I was asked to make another &#x2018;Terminator,&#x2019; I&#x2019;m not interested. I like Schwarzenegger a lot, but I&#x2019;d only make that film if the Terminator sat down and said he missed his mom.&#x201D;

Besson singled out some of the actors he has enjoyed working with the most, from Gary Oldman to ex-spouse Milla Jovovich and star of &#x201C;Dogman&#x201D; Caleb Landry Jones .

&#x201C;He&#x2019;s the genius of the decade. He&#x2019;s a very simple, very sober actor. He doesn&#x2019;t go out, doesn&#x2019;t do anything. But when he&#x2019;s on set, it&#x2019;s just wonderful. He&#x2019;ll try everything,&#x201D; he revealed.

During the presser, Besson said, &#x201C;If I could make all my films with [Caleb], that would be fantastic.&#x201D;

&#x201C;As for choosing actors in general, imagine you have to cross the Atlantic in a small boat with just one other person. Choose your partner well, or it will be really hard. Now, I work with actors who are, above all, good people. I don&#x2019;t want a star surrounded by 15 people.&#x201D;

Currently finishing an animated project that he produced and which will be released next year, Besson continues to collaborate with other directors.

&#x201C;If someone else could do it as well or better than me, I don&#x2019;t need to do it myself. I couldn&#x2019;t have done &#x2018;Taken&#x2019; any better. But &#x2018;The Big Blue&#x2019; was different. My parents were divers and I spent 15 years studying dolphins, so I wasn&#x2019;t going to leave that to anyone else. &#x2018;Dogman&#x2019; was the same thing. It was a story I was afraid someone else would ruin,&#x201D; he recalled.

&#x201C;Transporter&#x201D; was another hit for him as a producer.

&#x201C;One day, an agent I knew introduced me to a young actor, and I had a drink with Jason Statham. He seemed photogenic. I told him that if I had an idea, I&#x2019;d call him. I got on a plane and came up with the idea,&#x201D; he said.

&#x201C;We wrote it in a month and financed it in three. Louis Leterrier [who directed with Corey Yuen] was an assistant who wanted to start directing. I asked: &#x2018;Are you ready?&#x2019; Hollywood doesn&#x2019;t know how to do it anymore.&#x201D;

Recalling his beginnings, he said, &#x201C;We were a group of young people who couldn&#x2019;t get films made because the big studios controlled everything. So we said: &#x2018;Fine, we&#x2019;ll make them ourselves.&#x2019; Suddenly, there were no rules. For 30 years, we did whatever we wanted.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;Unfortunately, it&#x2019;s getting harder. That&#x2019;s a real shame because the films haven&#x2019;t exactly improved, that&#x2019;s for sure.&#x201D;

Reportedly working on a new sci-fi project , Besson still advocates the kind of cinema that allows people to escape reality.

&#x201C;At 14 or 15, I lived far from the city. I could see cows outside of my window, and I felt a strong urge to get away, so I started writing about a taxi pulling up outside my house and taking me off into space. I started writing &#x2018;The Fifth Element&#x2019; at 16 because it was my personal way of escaping.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Imagination is a muscle: the more you train it, the stronger it gets. It lets you explore worlds that don&#x2019;t exist, which is wonderful, because what does exist isn&#x2019;t that great. Especially right now.&#x201D;
